b/ref 17592186425836 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425839 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425842 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425844 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425848 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1077 "selection" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425848 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425850 1079 #uuid "b82a99f1-ae06-59b0-8b81-f9f50951a803" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425834 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425835 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425838 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425841 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425846 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1077 "selection" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425835 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425851 1079 #uuid "ed89a8ff-61ae-57a9-99b9-2c170ad6994b" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425852 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425850 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425852 1069 "q-129633" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425852 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425852 1071 "Suppose that $f(x,y)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(-2,0)=-3,\\,{f}_{x}(-2,0)=1,\\,{f}_{y}(-2,0)=0.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-2,0),$ estimate the value of $f(-1.99,0.01).$" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425852 1072 #uuid "3702a170-bd38-5307-a582-a3c4941c804b" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425852 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-2,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-2,0)+∇f(-2,0)\\cdot ⟨x-(-2),y-0⟩ \\\\  & =f(-2,0)+⟨{f}_{x}(-2,0),{f}_{y}(-2,0)⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,y⟩ \\\\  & =-3+⟨1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,y⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-1.99,0.01)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-1.99$ and $y=0.01,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.99,0.01) & ≈-3+⟨1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨-1.99+2,0.01⟩ \\\\  & =-3+⟨1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,0.01⟩ \\\\  & =-3+1(0.01)+0(0.01) \\\\  & =-3+0.01+0 \\\\  & =-2.99\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425853 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425849 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425853 1069 "q-98349" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425853 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425853 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0,3)=-9,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=y,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=x,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)=-2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,3),$ estimate the value of $f(0.98,-0.01,3.1).$" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425853 1072 #uuid "3e7afc5f-975b-58b4-8d28-e717181d277e" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425853 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,0,3)+∇f(1,0,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-0,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =-9+⟨{f}_{x}(1,0,3),{f}_{y}(1,0,3),{f}_{z}(1,0,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,0,3)$, ${f}_{y}(1,0,3)$ and ${f}_{z}(1,0,3),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,0,3) & =0 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,0,3) & =1 \\\\ {f}_{z}(1,0,3) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-9+⟨0,1,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(0.98,-0.01,3.1)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.98,y=-0.01$ and $z=3.1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.98,-0.01,3.1) & ≈-9+⟨0,1,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨0.98-1,-0.01,3.1-3⟩ \\\\  & =-9+⟨0,1,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.02,-0.01,0.1⟩ \\\\  & =-9-0.01-0.6 \\\\  & =-9.61\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425854 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425851 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425854 1069 "q-98327" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425854 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425854 1071 "Suppose that $f(x,y)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(3,-1)=-3,\\,{f}_{x}(3,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{y}(3,-1)=1.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(3.01,-0.97).$" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425854 1072 #uuid "bbf719bd-56e4-5b5f-a665-42577dad1834" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true] [17592186425854 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(3,-1)+∇f(3,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-3,y+1⟩ \\\\  & =f(3,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(3,-1),{f}_{y}(3,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y+1⟩ \\\\  & =-3+⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(3.01,-0.97)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=3.01$ and $y=-0.97,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.01,-0.97) & ≈-3+⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨3.01-3,-0.97+1⟩ \\\\  & =-3+⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,0.03⟩ \\\\  & =-3-0.01+0.03 \\\\  & =-2.98\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534563 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-18eb3038-8a37-56fa-9cf1-7cfec3b8c6d0" 17592186425834 "answer-223dc834-6cfc-5b40-b1db-14eab811390f" 17592186425835 "answer-36e5d885-03cb-556